**/0_never-push-this-dump-folder/
**/docs/
**/.codebuddy/
**/.workbuddy-ai/

# Deployment tooling metadata (contains project ids)
**/.vercel/

# Dependencies and generated output
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/coverage/

# Local environment and runtime files
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
**/*.log

# Supabase CLI local metadata
supabase/.temp/

# Temporary scratch / verification scratchpad (duplicates public assets)
**/.tmp-verify/

# Throwaway trees the image-format gate's own test builds under `backend/`.
# They are per-case sandboxes, created and removed by the suite; this stops a
# killed test run from leaving one staged.
**/.tmp-image-gate/

# The same, for the branch-source gate's test suite. Kept as its own line rather
# than a shared `**/.tmp-*/` so a new `.tmp-` directory cannot become invisible
# to git by accident — a scratch tree that silently stops being reported is how
# stray files reach a commit.
**/.tmp-branch-gate/

# Compiled output must never sit next to its TypeScript source. `shared-types`
# compiles src -> dist; stale `src/*.js` files were committed once, and any tool
# that prefers `.js` over `.ts` would silently resolve the stale build instead.
packages/shared-types/src/**/*.js

# Working documents that are deliberately kept off the remote. These are the
# manager's own planning files — the Geist font work, the outline/sentence-case
# work, and the Dashboard-as-Workspace structure pass. They are read locally and
# never pushed. Ignoring them (rather than just leaving them untracked) means a
# `git add -A` cannot sweep one into a commit by accident.
docs/geist-font-plan.md
docs/outline-and-case-plan.md
docs/dashboard-workspace-plan.md